1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,645
A score tells you what happened.

2
00:00:02,645 --> 00:00:04,850
It rarely tells you why.

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:09,700
Meet Touchline: football intelligence that makes the match easier to understand.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,669
This is the working overlay, replaying a fictional match at sixty times speed.

5
00:00:15,669 --> 00:00:18,722
A fixed seed makes the events reproducible.

6
00:00:18,722 --> 00:00:23,083
Each arriving action updates the score, chance map and statistics.

7
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:25,700
No historical match footage is needed.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,259
The shot map shows where chances came from.

9
00:00:29,259 --> 00:00:33,739
Select a marker to inspect the player, outcome and expected goals.

10
00:00:33,739 --> 00:00:36,998
Here, expected goals is an illustrative synthetic estimate.

11
00:00:36,998 --> 00:00:42,700
Momentum measures attacking progression from completed passes and carries, not the probability of winning.

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,419
The passing network turns individual actions into a team picture.

13
00:00:47,419 --> 00:00:52,281
Larger circles show greater involvement; thicker links show more completed passes.

14
00:00:52,281 --> 00:00:56,700
Switch teams to explore both sides of the same match.

15
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,898
Now ask a question in everyday language.

16
00:00:59,898 --> 00:01:06,108
Microsoft Agent Framework runs two stages: collect match evidence, then generate an answer with Gemini.

17
00:01:06,108 --> 00:01:09,834
The workflow checks event citations against the supplied context.

18
00:01:09,834 --> 00:01:17,700
A casual fan can ask about better chances; a more experienced viewer can explore field tilt and player involvement.

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,425
Every question captures the match at the current replay clock.

20
00:01:22,425 --> 00:01:25,522
Future events and final results are excluded.

21
00:01:25,522 --> 00:01:29,062
Answers show their snapshot time, while playback continues.

22
00:01:29,062 --> 00:01:33,488
This is grounded assistance, not a guarantee of perfect interpretation.

23
00:01:33,488 --> 00:01:35,700
Provider errors are shown explicitly.

24
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,212
For fans, Touchline adds context without leaving the screen.

25
00:01:40,212 --> 00:01:43,956
For streaming teams, it demonstrates interactive match intelligence.

26
00:01:43,956 --> 00:01:47,700
Production synchronization and Azure deployment remain next steps.

27
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,086
Touchline brings events, evidence and conversation together.

28
00:01:51,086 --> 00:01:57,700
From the first pass to the final chance: see the game, and understand the story.
